ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
candidate vertices considered=runners, gaps, fixed circle sections, section boundaries, wall-crossing events, residues, cover arcs, Fourier modes, matroid circuits, proof obligations, Boolean gates, automaton states, cocycle basis atoms, Lee-Yang root-motion ears
chosen vertices=proof gates and sidecar obligations
preserved predicate=residual packet progress to LRC14Statement through positive Phi/P, finite-address packets, observer-gluing certificates, or named state-lift debt
destroyed data=raw row identity, runner order, raw time, some owner history, and scalar maximizer labels unless a sidecar retains them

SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Circuit complexity is best used here as a uniform proof compiler: fixed inputs, declared fan-in/depth, missing-input vectors, and terminal proof exits.  The old endpoint/Phi/additive-circuit work supplies real gates, while the newer packet, automaton, cocycle, Lee-Yang, and Lean frontiers supply sidecars and legality checks.
